# Syntax: docs/LANGUAGE.md. Check with `rbb bid check`.
#
# Lead-directing doubles (`competitive.lead_directing_double.play`;
# convention-card competitive_bidding/lead_directing_doubles; Bridge
# Bum, "Lead Directing Double"; PBS btn/Lead_Directing_Double.btn):
# a double of an artificial bid asks partner to lead that suit. The
# hand: five cards with three of the top five honours, or six with two
# of the top three (the scenario's standard; Bridge Bum: a good suit).
#
# Written for the artificial bids the engine marks as such (`!rho.named(x)`:
# RHO has not bid the suit naturally), when it is RHO's call and our
# side has not bid:
#
# - responder's artificial bids over their 1NT or 2NT opening (Stayman,
#   transfers, minor-suit and other relays);
# - the 2♦ response to their strong 2♣;
# - an answer to their 4NT (keycard or ace ask).
#
# Not written: the Lightner double of a slam, doubles of their cue bids
# and of control bids (the engine marks few of those artificial), and
# the opening leader's actual lead (the engine does not play the cards).
# Notes: lead-directing-doubles.notes.md.

module lead-directing-doubles "Lead-directing doubles of artificial bids"
  needs  base
  skill  competitive_bidding/lead_directing_doubles
  card   competitive.lead_directing_double.play

define ldd_suit(x) = x>=5, top5(x)>=3 | (x>=6, quality(x)>=good)

after (1N) P (2x) | (1N) P (3x) | (2N) P (3x) | (4N) P (5x) when !rho.named(x)
  X   "Lead-directing: a good {x} suit, lead it"
      alert
      shows ldd_suit(x)
      priority 1
after (2C) P (2D) when !rho.named(D)
  X   "Lead-directing: a good diamond suit, lead it"
      alert
      shows ldd_suit(D)
      priority 1
